Example- to count the number of places

class Place{
    static int count = 0;
    Place(){
    count++;
  }
}

public class Main{
	public static void main(String[] args) {
	    new Place();
	    new Place();
	         System.out.println(Place.count);
    }


Why is main() Static?

public static void main(String[] args)

Java starts execution from main().

But before program starts: No object exists yet
Therefore Java cannot do:

Main m = new Main();
m.main();

So main() must belong to the class itself.





